## Frequently Asked Questions

### Q: Does Samsung have a built-in intruder selfie feature?
A: Not for the lock screen. Samsung's lock screen and theft protection settings lock the phone after wrong attempts, but none of them take a photo of the person or keep a list of attempts. You need an app like CrookCatcher for that.

### Q: How many wrong PIN attempts does a Samsung phone allow?
A: On phones that come with One UI 9, the waits start after 5 wrong guesses and the phone locks permanently on the 13th. After that, only a factory reset makes it usable again. Older phones and phones updated to One UI 9 follow their previous limits.

### Q: Will my Samsung erase itself after too many wrong attempts?
A: Only if **Auto factory reset** is turned on in Secure lock settings. On phones with One UI 9, running out of attempts doesn't erase the phone by itself, but you'll have to factory reset it to use it again.

### Q: Does CrookCatcher work with Samsung's fingerprint and face unlock?
A: Yes, you can keep using them. CrookCatcher reacts to a wrong PIN, pattern or password. Failed fingerprint or face attempts don't trigger it.

### Q: Will the person see that they were photographed?
A: CrookCatcher works in the background without a camera preview. Recent Android versions show a small indicator while the camera is in use; that's a system feature apps can't hide.

### Q: Why did CrookCatcher stop sending alerts on my Samsung?
A: Usually because Samsung put the app to sleep to save battery. Add it to **Never sleeping apps** (see step 5 above) and test again.

